# ThroughMark — approved vendor enablement sources (OPTIONAL).
# One host / GitHub org / URL-fragment per line; blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# A vendor-derived fence passes when its Source:/URL: CONTAINS any line below (substring match).
#
# Leaving ENABLEMENT_ALLOWLIST empty in the config means NO restriction — any qualifying vendor
# source is allowed. Use this file only if you deliberately want to pin to specific vendors; the
# guardrail's own qualification rules (vendor-published, public, licensed) still apply either way.
#
# Examples only — replace/delete; not an endorsement and not a limit on which vendors are allowed:
# github.com/<vendor-org>
# docs.<vendor>.com
# <vendor>.com
